schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-GATETRUTH
wu: E-GATETRUTH.W3
branch: wu/gate-truth/name-the-cause
tests:
  unit:
    count: 7
    covers: "git.rs: git_outcome keeps the exit disposition and both streams apart on a succeeding and a failing call; said() falls back to stdout for the `nothing to commit` case where git's one useful line is not on the stream it failed on; git_env's Err text is rebuilt from the raw outcome and compared, so every other caller's message is provably unchanged; git_outcome errs only when git cannot be spawned. mr.rs commit_verdict over the four quadrants: landed is a success whatever git exited (with the anomaly stated after the success line), did-not-move names git's own line and carries no success line, a zero exit that moved nothing states that contradiction, and no quadrant's verdict adds the commit message body or the argument vector - the fixture's git output deliberately does not mention the body, so the assertion is about what the code adds rather than what it was handed."
  integration:
    count: 16
    covers: "mr.rs (tests/mr.rs): mr commit lands and prints no error; a refusing commit-msg hook makes it exit non-zero printing the hook's stderr, omitting the body's second line and --cleanup=verbatim, with HEAD where it was; the built binary behind a git shim that execs real git then exits 1 after a commit reports success with the shim's stderr appended and HEAD really moved (the quadrant no hook can produce, because git ignores post-commit's exit status); a first commit lands from an unborn HEAD and a refused first commit is not a phantom landing (head_commit's None case). One authorisation test per leaf - no note, another schema, unparseable, a signed note whose signer the roster lists no key for (naming signer and roster path), a signed note listed only by an identity tier, a listed key over an amended tip, a base this repo does not hold, a bare note listed and unlisted - each asserting tip_authorised agrees with the enum. dod_gate.rs: the roster gap and the stale signature print different sentences, each naming its own cause and neither saying 'has no mr/v1 note' - the roster case asserts the roster's ABSOLUTE PATH, because NOT_AUTHORISED's closing line already contains the bare name; absent, unlisted and stale are pairwise unequal; an unreadable note says so; an unhashable base says the range cannot be recomputed; and every cause keeps the check id 8-manual-review with the receipt still listing manual-review."
  e2e:
    count: 1
    covers: "tests/mr.rs e2e_a_merge_judged_from_a_worktree_without_the_signers_key_says_so_and_lands_once_listed: .mr-allowed gitignored per DEC-10 (a committed roster would follow the checkout and the gap would never open), worktree A registers a key and signs a WU tip settled with the full test/v2, doc/v1 and cr notes the WU gate demands, worktree B - same .git, own working tree, no roster - is refused by the real pre-merge-commit hook with a message naming vuluu and B's own .mr-allowed path, then lands once B writes the key line. Hermetic: temp repo, temp worktree, throwaway ed25519 key, no network."
note: "E-GATETRUTH.W3 fixes P2a and P3, the two places the gate's verdict was right and its sentence sent the reader elsewhere. mr commit decides by whether HEAD moved rather than by git's exit code, and quotes git's own output instead of the message body; check 8 classifies an mr/v1 note into six leaves and prints the one it reached, naming the signer and this checkout's roster path for the worktree-local gap DEC-10's gitignored roster makes routine. tip_authorised is a matches! over the enum, so what authorises is unchanged. Regression proofs, each run on this branch: with mr_commit's tail reverted to git_env plus an unconditional Ok((0,..)), the two mr commit fixtures FAILED (53 of 55 passed); with check_manual_review reverted to the single sentence, 5 of the 6 new dod_gate fixtures FAILED (77 of 82 passed) - the sixth asserts the check id did not move and correctly passes both ways. Two review rounds each found a test that could not fail: round 1 the body-echo tautology (proved by reintroducing the P2a bug), round 2 the roster assertion satisfied by NOT_AUTHORISED's boilerplate (proved by dropping the roster path). Both are fixed and both now fail against the mutation that exposed them. Round 2's mutation finder also confirmed the rest bite: swapped verdict quadrants, a dropped anomaly sentence, an echoed body, a swapped said() fallback, swapped and collapsed leaves, and tip_authorised lying about a leaf are each caught by a named test. cargo test -p xtask --all-features green across every binary (lib 225, dod_gate 82, mr 58, e2e_design_flow 4, verify_doc 9, doc_hooks 8, gate0_cache 5, ui 2, debug_serve 1); cargo test --all-features green on the root package; cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -D warnings clean."
